okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Remote CRUD of the OAuth token list through the web interface and REST API while agents run; the temporary sign-in port must close after a timeout; reset/rotate the access API key and email/password web accounts from both the web interface and the CLI menu."
reported: "User, 2026-09-30: '현재 웹인터페이스와 rest api에 추가, 할기능. 외부에서 원격에서 oauth토큰의 리스트 crud 할수있도록. 그래서 동작중에도 백그라운드에서 변경할수있게. 또한 인증을 받으려고 오픈하는 임시 포트오픈이 특정 시간이 지난후까지 응답이 없으면 죽는것을 확인할것..접속에 필요한 api key와 사용자의 경우엔 (user email/pwd)을 리셋하거나 키로테이션하는것을 웹인터페이스뿐아니라. 커먼드라인의 메뉴 인터페이스에서도 할수있게해줄것'. Decision (asked): no email/password accounts existed, user chose '계정 기능 새로 구현'."
confirmed_before_change:
  web: "The web UI is the router itself (router_http.RouterHttpHandler); pages are Python-rendered; remote access = one admin bearer token (ROUTER_INSTANCE_DIR/router-external-token) with no rotation; no user accounts, password hashing or sessions anywhere."
  live_reads: "oauth_routing keeps one OAuthTokenStore per process but the store re-reads state and vault on every request, so API edits apply to the next routed request."
  port_timeout: "Loopback-only sign-in closed its listener after the timeout (callback.wait finally). The pasted-redirect path added in d924a56 blocked on input with the listener open indefinitely."
change:
  temp_port: "oauth_login.LoopbackCallback.expire_after(timeout) closes the listener on a timer during the paste wait; close() is idempotent."
  sign_in_split: "oauth_login.begin_sign_in / finish_sign_in (PendingSignIn); login() uses them; web sign-in needs no listener (Claude paste redirect uses fixed port 54545, Codex 1455)."
  accounts: "web_accounts.WebAccountStore at CONFIG_DIR/web-access (machine level): scrypt password hashes (n=2^14,r=8,p=1), sessions stored as SHA-256 of random tokens with 12 h TTL; password reset/removal revokes that account's sessions; files 0600; min password 8."
  router_auth: "RouterAccessPolicy.request_allowed takes session_allowed: a remote request passes with the admin bearer token or a live web session (cookie ciel_session, HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict, Secure behind https proxy; non-GET requires same Origin when an Origin header is present). Browsers without access get 303 to /ca/login; API clients keep 401 JSON. RouterExternalTokenRepository.rotate() replaces the file token (env-pinned tokens refuse)."
  rest: "GET /ca/login (public), POST /ca/auth/login|logout (public, 0.5 s delay on failure); GET /ca/admin (HTML); GET|POST /ca/oauth/tokens: list (no secrets), import (file contents), update (label, enabled), refresh, remove, sign_in_start -> authorize_url, sign_in_finish (pasted redirect, single use, 300 s expiry); GET|POST /ca/access: status (admin token hint only), add_account, reset_password, remove_account, revoke_sessions, rotate_admin_token (new value returned once)."
  ui: "web_access_ui: login page and admin page (tabs 'OAuth tokens' / 'Access', #access deep link); router home links 'Admin'."
  menu: "Main menu '16. Web access  [N accounts · admin token]': rotate admin token (confirm, shown once), add account (email, hidden password twice), per-account reset/remove, sign out every session."
  wiring: "router_http RouterHttpServices.access; ciel_runtime.py changed only on existing lines (still 4980)."
verification:
  unit: "tests/test_web_access.py (15): hashing/verify, account rules, reset/remove revoke sessions, session expiry, strict HttpOnly cookie and safe next, wrong password 401, cross-site POST refused, token CRUD without secrets, two-step web sign-in single use, access actions + rotation, policy session/admin-token/loopback, browser 303 vs API 401, rotate + env-pinned refusal, menu add/reset/remove, rotate only on confirm. tests/test_oauth_token_refresh.py: listener closes after timeout on both the callback path and the paste path; the paste-path test fails on the previous code ([True, True])."
  real_router_remote: "WSL real `ciel_runtime.py serve` bound 0.0.0.0 with external access, requests from the WSL eth0 address (non-loopback): browser GET /ca/admin -> 303 /ca/login?next=%2Fca%2Fadmin; API without auth 401; /ca/login 200; wrong password 401; right password -> cookie; import/disable/relabel while running -> state file shows ('renamed','disabled'); secret in API output 0; cross-site POST 401; old admin token 200 -> after rotation old 401, new 200; sign_in_start returns the authorize URL, expires_in 300; remove ok; password reset -> old session 401, new password 200; no plaintext password in web-access files."
  real_ui: "Headless Edge screenshots of /ca/admin (tokens table with Save label/Disable/Refresh/Remove, sign-in and import boxes), /ca/admin#access (admin token hint, rotate, accounts with reset/remove, add account, sign out all) and /ca/login."
  real_menu: "WSL tmux real menu: row '16. Web access  [0 accounts · admin token]'; add account with hidden password twice -> 'Added web account ops@example.com.'; rotate -> confirm 'yes' -> new token shown once and row hint updated."
  groups: "WSL: unit 1693 OK, router 1158 OK, channel 438 OK, runtime 323 OK; ruff clean; docs metadata check passed."
not_verified:
  - "A real provider sign-in completed through the web page (needs a person's account)."
  - "Browser clicks on the admin page (screenshots are rendered pages; actions were driven through the same REST calls with curl)."
notes:
  - "Loopback requests remain trusted without sign-in (existing policy); a same-host reverse proxy such as Tailscale Serve therefore still bypasses sign-in, as documented in docs/Remote-Bridge.md."
